.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 437 AM PDT Fri Aug 21 2026

Currently LIFR-VFR. Flight conditions will continue to deteriorate
through the morning; however, current flight categories should
prevail. With IFR stratus retreating to the coast this afternoon,
VFR is expected for all terminals except HAF. Relatively lower
confidence in the return of stratus tonight due to an increase in
wind and guidance/models showing clearing upstream this evening.
Nonetheless, the forecast leaned on persistence and the resilience
of the marine layer. Diurnal winds will prevail.

Vicinity of SFO...Currently IFR with southwesterly flow. High
confidence in VFR by this afternoon. Moderate confidence on
an IFR ceiling returning tonight. Diurnal winds will prevail.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Currently LIFR with northwesterly flow at
MRY and LIFR with westerly flow at SNS. Fog has recently developed
at MRY; therefore, there is low to moderate confidence that it`ll
reach SNS as the worst conditions are at the immediate coast. IFR
stratus will stick close to the coast this afternoon with another
return to LIFR conditions this evening. Diurnal winds will
prevail.

